Roots of |phi(B)|=0 and |theta(B)|=0 (moduli; > 1 is stationary/invertible):

  AR (Phi)          inf    1.17460    1.17460    1.55028 
  MA (Theta)    1.00000*   1.17493 

  * A root sits on the unit circle -- an MA root (modulus 1.00000).  The
    likelihood rose towards a non-invertible MA and the optimiser stopped
    at the engine's invertibility gate: this is a CONSTRAINED point, not an
    interior maximum.  The standard errors of the MA are not defined along
    that direction, and no LR that uses this fit has its usual
    distribution (BUG-49).
    The combination the model differences once too often -- the left
    null vector u of Theta*(1), smallest singular value 1.33e-01 -- has
    weights (|u|, on Ybar = [nabla Y2 ; W]):
      nabla muskrat        0.8015
      W1                   0.5981
    It mixes both blocks (nabla Y2 share 0.64, W share 0.36): no single
    reading; re-examine the rank and the orders before reading the
    estimates.


